## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to assemble a cohesive, beginner-friendly Azure stack with core services, PaaS patterns, security, monitoring, and basic DR.

## Key Concepts
- Static Web Apps, Functions (Consumption), Cosmos DB (SQL API)
- Front Door TLS endpoint, GitHub Actions CI/CD
- Application Insights, Azure Key Vault
- Tagging, budgets, basic cross-region DR

## Code Example
```javascript
// example: read a Key Vault secret with Azure SDK for JS
const { SecretClient } = require("@azure/keyvault-secrets");
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const client = new SecretClient("https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net", credential);
const secret = await client.getSecret("DbPassword");
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you optimize costs if traffic spikes unexpectedly?
- What monitoring metrics would you surface in dashboards and alerts?

## Why This Is Asked

This question validates end-to-end Azure architecture knowledge, including compute, data, observability, security, and disaster recovery fundamentals for a realistic entry-level cloud deployment.

## Key Concepts

- Azure Static Web Apps for SPA hosting with built-in CI/CD
- Azure Functions on Consumption plan for serverless API
- Azure SQL Database with geo-replication for data layer
- Application Insights instrumentation for Functions
- Log Analytics for centralized logging and querying
- Metric alerts for error rate monitoring
- Cost management with budget alerts
- Azure Front Door for TLS termination and global routing
- Basic cross-region DR using redundant services

